---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Docs — ubuos"
  description="How to install oss, connect your own project as a pack or an extension, and what every command does."
>
  <section>
    <p class="pill">Docs</p>
    <h1>The docs, in the order you need them.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Install the core, point it at your project, then look commands up as you go.
      Everything here is short on purpose — the CLI's own <code>--help</code> is the
      authority for flags, and these pages say what each piece is <em>for</em>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="tight">
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card">
        <h3><a href="/docs/start/">Getting started</a></h3>
        <p>
          From install to first review: token, <code>doctor</code>, first sync, first
          review — and the optional layers you can add later.
        </p>
        <p class="more"><a href="/docs/start/">Read →</a></p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3><a href="/docs/connect/">Connect your project</a></h3>
        <p>
          Build a <strong>pack</strong> so the engine can run your applications across
          your versions, or register an <strong>extension</strong> so <code>oss</code>
          can call a tool of your own.
        </p>
        <p class="more"><a href="/docs/connect/">Read →</a></p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3><a href="/docs/reference/commands/">Command reference</a></h3>
        <p>
          Every command, grouped by the question it answers, with what each one needs
          to run — a token, a local model, or nothing at all.
        </p>
        <p class="more"><a href="/docs/reference/commands/">Read →</a></p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tight">
    <h2>In the repositories</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      The longer-form documents live next to the code they describe, so they cannot
      drift without the diff showing it.
    </p>
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>The engine</h3>
        <p>What the runner is, the pack contract in full, and why POSIX only.</p>
        <p class="more"><a href="https://github.com/ramanathan1504/oss-cli/tree/main/runner">runner/README.md →</a></p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Setup and install, in depth</h3>
        <p>Tokens, keychains, note folders, local models — the optional layers.</p>
        <p class="more"><a href="https://github.com/ramanathan1504/oss-cli/blob/main/SETUP.md">SETUP.md →</a></p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>A finished pack to read</h3>
        <p>
          Nineteen real applications, seventy-three configurations, seven versions —
          the worked example the pack guide walks through.
        </p>
        <p class="more"><a href="https://github.com/ramanathan1504/log4j2-workout">log4j2-workout →</a></p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .tight { padding-top: 0; }
    .card h3 a { text-decoration: none; }
    .card h3 a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
    .more { margin-top: 12px; }
    .more a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 520; }
    .more a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  </style>
</Base>
